  "question": {
    "text": "A projectile A is thrown at an angle of $30^{\\circ}$ to the horizontal from point P. At the same time, another projectile $\\mathrm{B}$ is thrown with velocity $\\mathrm{v}_{2}$ upwards from the point $Q$ vertically below the highest point. For $\\mathrm{B}$ to collide with $\\mathrm{A}, \\frac{\\mathrm{v}_{2}}{\\mathrm{v}_{1}}$ should be\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/vF2xDXuYtbtwWbS7a7r-aDtGj8xqB_3Xt-aZ47JE_wU.original.fullsize.png\">",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "n6kkK",
      "text": "1",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "wgXCW",
      "text": "2",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Be6B8",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ersUP",
      "text": "4",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "This happen when vertical velocity of both are same.\r\n\r\n$\\therefore v_{2}=v_{1} \\sin 30^{\\circ} \\text { or } \\frac{v_{2}}{v_{1}}=\\frac{1}{2}$",
